    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d720-a1">

                <pb facs="0710" n="1444" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg1444"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No. 756.]</seg></opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Admiral Selfridge to
                        Mr. Terrell.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">U.
                                S. S. San Francisco</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Smyrna, Asia
                                Minor</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1895-12-25"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">December 25,
                    1895</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose you a letter
                    from Moustapha Zehni Pasha, the vali of Aleppo.</p>
                <p>You will see that not only he denies that the mission buildings at Marash were
                    set on fire by Turkish soldiers, as intimated by Mr. Lee in his narrative of the
                    events that took place at Marash, but the vali adds that a testimonial of
                    satisfaction was given to the Turkish commander by the American
                    missionaries.</p>
                <p>Very respectfully,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Thos. O. Selfridge</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Rear-Admiral, U. S. N.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
